# winoracle 2026-09-28, WARP, FL 11_1, x64 (x86 identical up to printf rounding).
# Vitreo verdicts (compare with a 1.0/255 tolerance for filtering):
#  M1 WRAP/MIRROR/CLAMP/BORDER/MIRROR_ONCE, point + linear: CORRECT
#  M2 all 9 filters x LOD: CORRECT except point-mip selection at an exact
#     .5 LOD (spec 7.18.10: floor(LOD+0.5) -> LOD 0.5 = mip 1; Metal mip 0)
#  M3 MinMaxFiltering: Vitreo reports 0 (WARP 1), refuses the mixed
#     MINIMUM_/MAXIMUM_ filters (E_NOTIMPL) but ACCEPTS MINIMUM_/MAXIMUM_
#     MIN_MAG_MIP_LINEAR and _ANISOTROPIC and returns a plain average: FABRICATED
#  M4 comparison, every func, point + PCF on R32_FLOAT: CORRECT; border
#     red 0/1: CORRECT; border red 0.5: E_NOTIMPL (MISSING)
#     (depth-texture rows: the CopyResource into the depth texture reads 0 -- area 06)
#  M5 custom border colours on s0..s7 (PS and CS), fewer-channel formats: CORRECT;
#     on s8..s15: WRONG (transparent black / format default);
#     A8_UNORM with (0,0,0,1): WRONG (alpha 0); B5G6R5 textures: unsupported (area 08)
#  M6 MipLODBias on SampleLevel / SampleGrad / SampleCmpLevelZero: WRONG
#     (not applied; spec 7.18.11, 22.4.18, 22.4.20); MinLOD/MaxLOD clamps,
#     mag/min after clamp: CORRECT; MinLOD > MaxLOD: E_INVALIDARG (Windows
#     accepts, MinLOD wins -> mip 3)
#  M7 anisotropy: CORRECT within tolerance
